  "body": "From https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5334#issuecomment-648879591:\r\n\r\n> I noticed that `multipart/x-mixed-replace` also invokes \"process a navigate response\" and can do so from a top-level browsing context. Those subsequent responses should never be allowed to change COOP+COEP state I think, but this is not specified now. We might also not have test coverage there, because it's in general a somewhat buggy part of the whole navigation algorithm.",
